{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1215602-additions-to-a-dragon-s-library","id":1215602,"title":"Additions to a Dragon's library","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-05-05T15:09:58-07:00","id":1215602,"title":"Additions to a Dragon's library","content":"So, I have a new player who has started with a character in the Ordo. She asked about the library, because, well, scholars should have a library. Luckily, when I started the game some years ago, I started a list of books in the library, running from the mundane academic to the esoteric, containing both real world books and fictional volumes. I delved into the files and pulled out the list. Her eyes bugged when I gave it to her, and the next evening she sent me a list of books she was pulling from the shelves. So that got me in the mood to add more books to the stacks.<br /> <br /> So, if you have titles of treatises, tomes, journals, or texts of relevance to the studies of Dragons or other scholar, could you put them in this thread? I'd appreciate the ideas.<br /> <br /> Also, here is a copy of the library which you can mine for your own games:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1uo_YbzHaG-K5tJ9bx16S93JQfCw2TBOjgdCUERW0djA/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Vancouver Library</a><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2203-corrigan","name":"Corrigan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-05T17:53:18-07:00","id":1215633,"title":"","content":"Here\u2019s my $.0.2 (all of the following is fictional):<br /> <i>The Black Book</i>, a fictional medieval Voynich Manuscript-style codex, full of obscure alchemical imagery and a written in a language seemingly impervious to translation. (High Speech? Possibly!)<br /> <i>Book of Doors</i>, a tome deemed too dangerous to even <i>look</i> at, kept under paranoid levels of security, written in the era of Zoroastrian Persia. Merely glancing through it brings on blinding headaches; actually READING the thing leads to sanity-shattering nightmares.<br /> <i>Brownton List Folio</i>, a slender tome from the Renaissance, written in a code long ago broken, that lists the supposed names of \u2018daimons\u2019 and how they may be bound.<br /> <i>Kant\u2019s Theorum of Worlds</i>, a (highly flawed and very inaccurate) treatise on supernatural cosmology, from the 1920s.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12219,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","user":"Demigod Beast","date":". 05-05-2018, 09:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-05T19:20:18-07:00","id":1215650,"title":"","content":"The Four Books and Five Classics - compiled by Confucius with commentary by some of his followers, these are the canon texts of Confucianism. The link below has a brief summary of each book. I Ching, Classic of Poetry, and Classic of Rites are likely to be of primary interest to the psuedoscientific and mystical pursuits used by the typical presentation of the Ordo Dracul.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.china-expats.com/ChineseLiterature2.htm\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"http://www.china-expats.com/Nav/Home_up.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.china-expats.com/ChineseLiterature2.htm\" target=\"_blank\"> The Four Books and Five Classics </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.china-expats.com/ChineseLiterature2.htm\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.china-expats.com/ChineseLiterature2.htm </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Chinese literature, Confusian literature, four books and five classics, includes the I-Ching or Book of Changes </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The Art of War - Sun Tzu one of the most influential texts about military and legal warfare to date<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://classics.mit.edu/Tzu/artwar.html\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"http://classics.mit.edu/Images/home-icon.gif\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://classics.mit.edu/Tzu/artwar.html\" target=\"_blank\"> The Internet Classics Archive | The Art of War by Sun Tzu </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://classics.mit.edu/Tzu/artwar.html\" target=\"_blank\"> http://classics.mit.edu/Tzu/artwar.html </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> The Art of War by Sun Tzu, part of the Internet Classics Archive </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The Hundred Schools of Thought were a collection of treatises and schools of thought on a variety of intellectual, philosophical, and cultural subjects in ancient China. Many of the writings and sometimes even their authors were destroyed during the Qin Dynasty and would be an excellent time frame to insert forgeries or &quot;lost&quot; texts. The link below has a summary of some of the writings to survive.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.newworldencyclopedia.org/entry/Hundred_Schools_of_Thought\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"http://www.newworldencyclopedia.org/images/nwe_header.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.newworldencyclopedia.org/entry/Hundred_Schools_of_Thought\" target=\"_blank\"> Hundred Schools of Thought - New World Encyclopedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.newworldencyclopedia.org/entry/Hundred_Schools_of_Thought\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.newworldencyclopedia.org/entry/Hundred_Schools_of_Thought </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> I will add more later.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-09T09:00:30-07:00","id":1217011,"title":"","content":"I always abstract these things so I'm not much use here, but this is a cool idea.<br /> <br /> I think any of Aleister Crowley works would make sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-09T09:58:40-07:00","id":1217035,"title":"","content":"The Malacetic Atlas and the Atlas Obscura (actual book) could be handy for a dragon.<br /> Strange Highways: A guidebook to American Mysteries and the Unexplained (actual book)<br /> may be the Voynich Manuscript?<br /> I know the dead sea scrolls have been scanned and are available online.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1776-sidious","name":"Sidious","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1776_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-09T10:49:18-07:00","id":1217046,"title":"","content":"I notice the lack of I<br /> Sir Isaac Newton's Principia, he was into alchemy and the occult.<br /> On the vampire writer side of things don't forget that academic disputes could be played out over published works. As an example a Mekhet might publish a paper on how Vitae requirements of clan Disaplins affects behaviour (and ethics) and end up in an ongoing dispute with a Ventrue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-09T10:58:34-07:00","id":1217050,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the input so far. I will update as time and computer access allow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2203-corrigan","name":"Corrigan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}